      ],
      "text": "A SYNTHETIC BOOK",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0002",
      "page": 0,
      "bbox": [
        508,
        300,
        693,
        328
      ],
      "text": "A Synthetic Book",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0003",
      "page": 0,
      "bbox": [
        243,
        340,
        1041,
        369
      ],
      "text": "This book exists to exercise the exporter end to end, and it is set",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0004",
      "page": 0,
      "bbox": [
        199,
        380,
        1000,
        407
      ],
      "text": "out the way a printed book is set out, with paragraphs that run for",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0005",
      "page": 0,
      "bbox": [
        200,
        420,
        1001,
        448
      ],
      "text": "several lines before they turn. It raises a question of paragraphs",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0006",
      "page": 0,
      "bbox": [
        201,
        460,
        999,
        489
      ],
      "text": "and it answers that question in the only way the pipeline is willing",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0007",
      "page": 0,
      "bbox": [
        199,
        500,
        810,
        527
      ],
      "text": "to answer it, which is from the evidence on the page.",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0008",
      "page": 0,
      "bbox": [
        242,
        540,
        1043,
        568
      ],
      "text": "The far-right press and the far-right movement are named here more",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0009",
      "page": 0,
      "bbox": [
        201,
        580,
        999,
        609
      ],
      "text": "than once, so that the compound is attested somewhere in the book",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0010",
      "page": 0,
      "bbox": [
        199,
        620,
        1000,
        647
      ],
      "text": "that is not the line where it happens to be broken. That is the",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0011",
      "page": 0,
      "bbox": [
        200,
        660,
        1001,
        688
      ],
      "text": "whole of the evidence the joiner is allowed to use, and it is the",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0012",
      "page": 0,
      "bbox": [
        201,
        700,
        901,
        729
      ],
      "text": "reason a compound survives the export with its hyphen intact.",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0013",
      "page": 0,
      "bbox": [
        241,
        740,
        1042,
        767
      ],
      "text": "A paragraph can run to the very foot of a page and carry on at the",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0014",
      "page": 0,
      "bbox": [
        200,
        780,
        1001,
        808
      ],
      "text": "top of the next one, and when it does the sentence is not finished",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0015",
      "page": 0,
      "bbox": [
        201,
        820,
        999,
        849
      ],
      "text": "and the reader should never hear a full stop where the page merely",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0016",
      "page": 0,
      "bbox": [
        199,
        860,
        1000,
        887
      ],
      "text": "ran out of room. Sometimes the turn falls inside a word, like ques-",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0056",
      "page": 0,
      "bbox": [
        580,
        1680,
        621,
        1708
      ],
      "text": "12",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0017",
      "page": 1,
      "bbox": [
        460,
        90,
        741,
        118
      ],
      "text": "A SYNTHETIC BOOK",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0018",
      "page": 1,
      "bbox": [
        201,
        220,
        999,
        249
      ],
      "text": "tion, which the book itself can prove should be rejoined, because it",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0019",
      "page": 1,
      "bbox": [
        199,
        260,
        649,
        287
      ],
      "text": "has used that word elsewhere as a word.",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0057",
      "page": 1,
      "bbox": [
        581,
        1680,
        619,
        1709
      ],
      "text": "13",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0020",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        460,
        90,
        741,
        118
      ],
      "text": "A SYNTHETIC BOOK",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0021",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        538,
        340,
        663,
        369
      ],
      "text": "Chapter One",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0022",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        199,
        500,
        522,
        527
      ],
      "text": "A Heading That Sits In Place",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0023",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        200,
        620,
        466,
        648
      ],
      "text": "A Subheading Beneath It",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0024",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        243,
        660,
        1041,
        689
      ],
      "text": "The first paragraph of the chapter runs on for a good few lines so",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0025",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        199,
        700,
        1000,
        727
      ],
      "text": "that it reads as prose rather than as a label, and so that the body",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0026",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        200,
        740,
        1001,
        768
      ],
      "text": "of the book is what sets the measure and the leading against which",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0027",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        201,
        780,
        999,
        809
      ],
      "text": "everything else on the page is judged. Nothing here is a constant.",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0028",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        199,
        820,
        706,
        847
      ],
      "text": "Every threshold is derived from these lines.",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0029",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        242,
        860,
        1043,
        888
      ],
      "text": "A second paragraph follows the first, opening the way this book",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0030",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        201,
        900,
        999,
        929
      ],
      "text": "opens its paragraphs and no other way, because a book commits to a",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0031",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        199,
        940,
        1000,
        967
      ],
      "text": "convention and holds to it. Whichever convention that is, it is the",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0032",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        200,
        980,
        1001,
        1008
      ],
      "text": "one the calibration pass has to find, and the one the grouping pass",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0033",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        201,
        1020,
        751,
        1049
      ],
      "text": "then reads. The two are not allowed to disagree.",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0034",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        199,
        1060,
        1000,
        1087
      ],
      "text": "A quoted passage sits here, set apart from the body text around it,",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0035",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        200,
        1100,
        1001,
        1128
      ],
      "text": "and it is its own category, so a paragraph never flows across the",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0036",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        201,
        1140,
        763,
        1169
      ],
      "text": "boundary between it and the prose on either side.",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0037",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        199,
        1180,
        672,
        1207
      ],
      "text": "Figure 1. A caption belonging to a plate.",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0038",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        200,
        1220,
        362,
        1248
      ],
      "text": "The first item",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0039",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        201,
        1260,
        372,
        1289
      ],
      "text": "The second item",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0040",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        199,
        1300,
        361,
        1327
      ],
      "text": "The third item",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0041",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        200,
        1520,
        684,
        1548
      ],
      "text": "1. A footnote at the foot of its own page.",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0058",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        579,
        1680,
        620,
        1707
      ],
      "text": "14",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0042",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        461,
        90,
        739,
        119
      ],
      "text": "A SYNTHETIC BOOK",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0043",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        536,
        340,
        664,
        367
      ],
      "text": "Chapter Two",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0044",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        242,
        380,
        1043,
        408
      ],
      "text": "The second chapter opens on a word that the compositor split as far-",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0045",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        201,
        420,
        999,
        449
      ],
      "text": "right, which must keep the hyphen it was written with, because this",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0046",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        199,
        460,
        1000,
        487
      ],
      "text": "book uses that compound elsewhere and never uses the welded form.",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0047",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        200,
        500,
        1001,
        528
      ],
      "text": "Getting that backwards is not a typo in the output; it is a word the",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0048",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        201,
        540,
        935,
        569
      ],
      "text": "author never wrote, and the reader cannot tell what it replaced.",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0049",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        241,
        580,
        1042,
        607
      ],
      "text": "Another paragraph mentions a zeb-",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0050",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        200,
        620,
        1001,
        648
      ],
      "text": "ruck, which nothing in this book attests either way, so the hyphen",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0051",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        201,
        660,
        999,
        689
      ],
      "text": "stays there too. An unproven pair keeps what was printed, because",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0052",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        199,
        700,
        821,
        727
      ],
      "text": "that is the direction a reader can still recover from.",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0053",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        200,
        740,
        500,
        768
      ],
      "text": "TEXT READ OFF A PHOTOGRAPH",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0054",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        201,
        780,
        510,
        809
      ],
      "text": "a leak from the facing page",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0055",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        199,
        1520,
        706,
        1547
      ],
      "text": "2. A second footnote, on the second chapter.",
      "conf": 92,
      "psm": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "l0059",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        580,
